# https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0041 (Manage secrets)
# democratic-csi controller requires secret read access for CSI sidecars to fetch storage backend credentials
KSV-0041
AVD-KSV-0041

# https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0005 (SYS_ADMIN capability added)
# CSI node daemonset requires SYS_ADMIN capability to attach, partition, format, and mount iSCSI block devices
KSV-0005
AVD-KSV-0005

# https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0008 (Access to host IPC namespace)
# CSI node daemonset requires host IPC access to communicate with host storage subsystem
KSV-0008
AVD-KSV-0008

# https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0009 (Access to host network)
# CSI node daemonset requires host network access for direct iSCSI portal communication and target discovery
KSV-0009
AVD-KSV-0009

# https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0010 (Access to host PID)
# CSI node daemonset requires host PID access to execute iscsiadm via nsenter against host processes
KSV-0010
AVD-KSV-0010

# https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0014 (Root file system is not read-only)
# CSI node and controller components maintain runtime state, sockets, and logs on the container root filesystem
KSV-0014
AVD-KSV-0014

# https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0017 (Privileged)
# CSI node daemonset requires privileged mode to perform host-level kernel block device operations and mounts
KSV-0017
AVD-KSV-0017

# https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0118 (Default security context configured)
# Upstream CSI controller sidecars and node driver run with driver-specific security profiles rather than restricted baseline
KSV-0118
AVD-KSV-0118

# https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0121 (Kubernetes resource with disallowed volumes mounted)
# CSI node daemonset requires hostPath volume mounts (/dev, /sys, /var/lib/kubelet, /var/iscsi) to manage host storage and mounts
KSV-0121
AVD-KSV-0121

# https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0001 (Can elevate its own privileges)
# CSI node and controller containers require privilege escalation to manipulate block storage devices and run storage utilities
KSV-0001
AVD-KSV-0001

# https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0012 (Runs as root user)
# CSI driver and Kubernetes-SIG storage sidecars must run as root to interact with host mounts, block devices, and sockets
KSV-0012
AVD-KSV-0012

# https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0013 (Image tag ":latest" used)
# False positive triggered by subchart template defaults when rendered without override
KSV-0013
AVD-KSV-0013

# https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0022 (Specific capabilities added)
# CSI node daemonset requires specific Linux capabilities (SYS_ADMIN) to manage host mounts and devices
KSV-0022
AVD-KSV-0022

# https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0023 (hostPath volumes mounted)
# CSI node daemonset requires hostPath volume mounts to communicate with the kubelet plugin registration socket and host paths
KSV-0023
AVD-KSV-0023

# https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0104 (Seccomp policies disabled)
# CSI node and controller containers require unconfined or default seccomp profiles to execute privileged storage operations
KSV-0104
AVD-KSV-0104

# https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0003 (Default capabilities: some containers do not drop all)
# CSI node and controller containers retain Linux capabilities necessary for storage driver and kernel communication
KSV-0003
AVD-KSV-0003

# https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0004 (Default capabilities: some containers do not drop any)
# Upstream CSI sidecar containers and node driver do not drop capabilities by default to preserve block device access
KSV-0004
AVD-KSV-0004

# https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0007 (Manages /etc/hosts)
# False positive triggered by subchart container template definitions
KSV-0007
AVD-KSV-0007

# https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0015 (CPU requests not specified)
# Upstream CSI sidecars intentionally leave CPU unconstrained to avoid volume provisioning and attach latency
KSV-0015
AVD-KSV-0015

# https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0016 (Memory requests not specified)
# Upstream CSI sidecars intentionally leave memory unconstrained to prevent OOM errors during volume lifecycle operations
KSV-0016
AVD-KSV-0016

# https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0030 (Runtime/Default Seccomp profile not set)
# CSI node and controller sidecars require custom/unconfined seccomp profiles for kernel storage system calls
KSV-0030
AVD-KSV-0030

# https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ksv-0106 (Container capabilities must only include NET_BIND_SERVICE)
# CSI containers require storage and system management capabilities beyond NET_BIND_SERVICE
KSV-0106
AVD-KSV-0106
